INT. SYNERGY DEPARTMENT - FORMER FUNERAL HOME - MORNING

Cubicles line the old viewing room. A faux-brass chandelier. A banner reads "WE'RE ALL FAMILY HERE." Coffins serve as supply cabinets.

MR. PELLINGHAM (50s, bow tie, sweating) stands on a velvet kneeler holding a clipboard. GLORIA (40s, reading glasses on a chain) sorts paperclips. SPUD (30s, hoodie) eats cereal from a casket lid. ADAEZE (20s, headset, razor eyes) types without looking.

MR. PELLINGHAM
People! People! Today we pivot.

GLORIA
We pivoted yesterday, Mr. Pellingham.

SPUD
Twice. Before lunch.

MR. PELLINGHAM
Spud, today we pivot to a pivot.

ADAEZE
Is that a metric?

MR. PELLINGHAM
Adaeze, it's a mindset.

GLORIA
What happened to the mindset?

SPUD
It got laid off.

MR. PELLINGHAM
Nobody got laid off. We are right-sizing the horizon.

ADAEZE
Gloria, did he say horizon?

GLORIA
He said horizon.

MR. PELLINGHAM
I am going to need everyone's quarterly aspirations by noon.

SPUD
Mr. Pellingham, I only have a quarterly nap.

GLORIA
Spud!

ADAEZE
Put it in the shared folder.

MR. PELLINGHAM
Thank you, Adaeze.

SPUD
He thanked her. Mark the calendar.

GLORIA
Mark it. Under "Funeral".

Mr. Pellingham looks at the banner. Climbs down. Sighs.

MR. PELLINGHAM
Friends, let's just have cake.

SPUD
Is it from the last funeral?

MR. PELLINGHAM
It's... lemon.
